  "conclusions": [
    "Amu #1428 and #1446 retain Node bin/amu and NBB bin/kotoba entries at the fetched public heads.",
    "Their canonical package/bootstrap source still spawns cc and the lineage C loader; a .kotoba file alone does not establish a C-free build.",
    "Amu #1446 improves the locked guest-source farm; its successful Linux seed workflow runs a C loader and is not a qualified loaderless product compiler.",
    "Amu #1323 proposes a locked browser-Wasm route but retains hosted public launchers and C-loader build/qualification drivers.",
    "Native #204 is a partial compiler source port. Native #205 contains loaderless runtime source candidates but no tracked compiler/runtime binary at the fetched head.",
    "Native #205 exact-head PR workflow query returned no runs; this is not a passing build or runtime verdict.",
    "No qualified selfhost-built loaderless compiler entry was established from the inspected candidates. Actual compilation gates remain unmet."
  ],
